# "Target creature you own" is about ownership, not control (CR 108.3, 108.4): Bot2's Thieving Skydiver has taken Bot1's
# Ornithopter, and Bot1's has taken Bot2's. Bot1's Eagles may not choose the Ornithopter Bot1 controls but Bot2 owns (the
# refusal), and may choose the one Bot2 controls but Bot1 owns; it goes to its owner's hand, Bot1's, and counts for a Bird.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Black Lotus
Thieving Skydiver
Ornithopter
The Eagles Are Coming!
Mox Sapphire
Mox Pearl
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Thieving Skydiver
Ornithopter
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot2.Hand.Thieving Skydiver.Cast(Kicked: 1)
Bot2.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot2.Battlefield = Island; Ornithopter; Ornithopter; Thieving Skydiver
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Thieving Skydiver.Cast(Kicked: 1)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield = Plains; Mox Sapphire; Mox Pearl; Thieving Skydiver; Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.The Eagles Are Coming!.Cast
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Ornithopter; Plains
Bot1.Battlefield = Plains; Mox Sapphire; Mox Pearl; Thieving Skydiver; Ornithopter; Bird Soldier Token
Bot2.Battlefield = Island; Thieving Skydiver
Bot2.Graveyard = Black Lotus
